  "message.6bba8f5166d2": "Mana spent",
  "message.e53997b9fb4a": "How Crux works",
  "message.490116755628": "{arg0}: here, Confront is",
  "message.4d6cd018d002": ", Deflect is",
  "message.4cdbaaaa2c2c": ", and Push for crux is",
  "message.39e889f89956": ". The words change with the meeting; the rules never do.",
  "message.b6681148102f": "They hold one",
  "message.063177344254": "Push for crux",
  "message.71c88c977ca7": "at the chance shown: if it lands, you win. The first push costs",
  "message.00db79ac5937": "1 of their Patience",
  "message.885f45514c4e": ", the next 2, then 3 and so on, and a push may overdraw it: a landed push wins even past zero. A miss costs nothing more.",
  "message.15fc80de7870": "Meanwhile they raise",
  "message.4ae0604ff113": "small arguments",
  "message.10d111d6e4c7": ", {arg4} on the table at a time, from a deck made for this kind of meeting.",
  "message.4a017eda7089": "one (a check at the chance shown) or",
  "message.40dccc491961": "Deflect",
  "message.27491c06ee77": "it, for",
  "message.109ee0c7ef6a": "1 Patience",
  "message.3788b762783b": ". Either way it leaves the table and the next is dealt.",
  "message.8b7f8b37f784": "Each argument shows its stakes exactly:",
  "message.b429f2a34b28": "▲ crux +x%",
  "message.4a604bea8cb4": "if you win it, and",
  "message.659ad6a10490": "what failing costs, which differs by argument: Suspicion, the crux cooling, more Patience, the others rallying, Mana, crowns, Health, or it coming back later.",
  "message.7138e3ba1493": "Neglect an argument too long and it lands",
  "message.66fb008e4ccb": ": you take its failure’s cost anyway. Most wait 3 to 5 of your actions; an",
  "message.1b015904cc17": "Urgent",
  "message.73f40e17cb40": "one, 1 or 2. Each card counts down (",
  "message.72f49347b4dc": "neglected in 3",
  "message.8501b9ca3531": "). Deflect the ones you can’t win before they land.",
  "message.8c154f1307a0": "They have {arg5} Patience. Build the crux up, then pick your moment to go all-in. At zero, the meeting is over. {arg6} Suspicion and they walk out: failures and spells both add to it.",
  "message.2dc2930952ed": "Some are",
  "message.ef9d7e1e5b52": ": crowns, Health, Renown or a spell cast for them. Meet one and Confronting it is certain (you pay what it asks); if you can’t, it fails. Each card’s icon shows what it tests or asks.",
  "message.a8c68a3a327a": "About one argument in six does something more, shown on a banner across it: a",
  "message.9b64c1c869ad": "Sore point",
  "message.a9414977ca56": "bars the crux until you answer it, an",
  "message.f4b13e93df07": "Opening",
  "message.f54f0cbc183f": "makes your next push free when you win it, a",
  "message.b02a1c419948": "Watchful",
  "message.4c5eae0669af": "one makes every spell cost more Suspicion while it stands, and so on.",
  "message.12eccfc7ce4b": ", at the Mana prices shown. Each breaks one rule over the whole table (Foresight rolls every argument’s dice before you choose, Haste confronts them all at once, Seal clears the table), and",
  "message.9f9e640289c2": "every cast is seen: +1 Suspicion",
  "message.768c36c4090a": "(Foresight and Haste +2), shown in the tile’s corner. A spell that would make them walk out can’t be cast. Pick a spell to see exactly what it would do; pick it again, or Cast.",
  "message.97b39ebac2f0": "In a few informal meetings they have magic too: one of their arguments is",
  "message.b358c76f7d35": "their spell",
  "message.6eee131435fa": ". It can’t be deflected.",
  "message.a5e2acc1652d": "it (an Arcana check; it stays if you fail) or counter it with",
  "message.b311172dd9a4": "Ward",
  "message.9bd75a3fb14a": "Reflect",
